{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "55255f16-0ce8-4958-bb1b-7ebeb4dbe24d",
    "name": "MarQ Agent API",
    "description": "Conversational access to the MyTAI CRM, plus a per-user workspace for uploaded files.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Start the API:  `python main.py`\n2. Mint a token:   `python scripts/dev_token.py mint`\n3. Paste it into the `token` environment variable.\n\nSelect the **MarQ Agent \u2014 local** environment before sending anything.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Auth is Bearer at the collection level; every request inherits it.\n- `thread_id` and `file_id` are captured automatically by test scripts, so run *Ask a question* before the Threads folder.\n- The identity (`requester_id`, `workspace_id`) comes from the token and is refused if sent in a body \u2014 see **Negative tests**.\n- **SSE:** Postman buffers `text/event-stream` rather than showing live frames. Use `curl -N` to watch a stream properly; the command is in the *Ask a question (streaming)* description.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000"
    },
    {
      "key": "thread_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "file_id",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Unauthenticated probes.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Does no I/O and needs no token. A liveness probe that touches the database restarts a healthy process when a dependency blips.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"ok\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"ok\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health/ready",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "ready"
              ]
            },
            "description": "What is actually reachable, not what is configured.\n\n`vector_index` reports false when Qdrant is not running \u2014 that is expected here and does NOT block readiness: search degrades while reconciliation and the CRM agent keep working.\n\n`checkpointer` false means conversations would not survive a restart.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"reports every component\", () => {",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  [\"database\",\"checkpointer\",\"model\",\"vector_index\"].forEach(k => pm.expect(b).to.have.property(k));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Chat",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Ask a question",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/chat",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "chat"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Runs a full turn and waits for the answer. Takes a few seconds \u2014 two to three model calls.\n\nGround truth on the dev fixture: **315** deals.\n\nCaptures `thread_id` into the environment, so the next requests continue this conversation.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"How many deals are there in total?\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"thread_id\", b.thread_id);",
                  "pm.test(\"answered\", () => pm.expect(b.answer).to.not.be.empty);",
                  "pm.test(\"routed\", () => pm.expect([\"deals\",\"leads\",\"workspace\",\"out_of_scope\"]).to.include(b.route));",
                  "console.log(\"route:\", b.route, \"| tools:\", b.tools_used);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Follow-up (same thread)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/chat",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "chat"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Proves conversation memory. Because checkpoints live in PostgreSQL, this works even if you restart the server between the two requests \u2014 try it.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"What number did you just tell me?\",\n  \"thread_id\": \"{{thread_id}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "console.log(pm.response.json().answer);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Ask a question (streaming)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/chat/stream",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "chat",
                "stream"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Server-Sent Events: `start`, `route`, `tool`, many `token`, then `final`.\n\n**Postman buffers this** and shows one blob at the end rather than live frames. To watch it properly:\n\n```\ncurl -N -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/stream \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $(python scripts/dev_token.py mint)\" \\\n  -d '{\"message\":\"Which franchise has the most cancellations?\"}'\n```\n\nThe routing decision and the SQL the agent generates are filtered out before they reach the wire.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Which franchise has the most cancellations?\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"streams SSE\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include(\"event: final\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"never leaks generated SQL\", () => {",
                  "  const tokens = pm.response.text().split(\"\\n\")",
                  "    .filter(l => l.startsWith(\"data:\"))",
                  "    .map(l => { try { return JSON.parse(l.slice(5)).text || \"\"; } catch (e) { return \"\"; } })",
                  "    .join(\"\");",
                  "  pm.expect(tokens).to.not.include(\"SELECT\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Out of scope",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/chat",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "chat"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Declines in one line without spending a database round-trip. `route` comes back as `out_of_scope`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"What is the weather in Cairo today?\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"declined\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().route).to.eql(\"out_of_scope\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
